		"@okikio/html": {
			"module_doc": {
				"doc": "Parse imperfect HTML and query it through one consistent tree adapter. A selector library and a parser with incompatible trees can silently return no matches even when the element exists.\n\nSelect elements for discovery, read attributes and text, then inspect source locations for evidence or rewriting. Resolve relative URLs against the fetched page URL in your application. Parsing does not run scripts or fetch subresources. The parsed tree is process-local data; share a serializable projection with a Worker rather than treating DOM identity as a wire contract.\n",
				"tags": [
					{
						"kind": "example",
						"doc": "```ts\nimport * as html from '@okikio/html';\nconst page = html.parse('<main><a href=\"/guide\">Read the guide</a></main>');\nconst link = html.selectOne(page.document, 'main a[href]');\nconsole.log(link === null ? 'missing' : html.attribute(link, 'href'));\nconsole.log(link === null ? 'missing' : html.text(link));\n```\n"
					},
					{
						"kind": "module"
					}
				]
			},
